---
import BaseHead from "../components/BaseHead.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import RelayDemo from "../components/RelayDemo.astro";
import { RELAY_BASE, SITE_TITLE } from "../consts";

const create = `curl -X POST ${RELAY_BASE}/v1/schedules \\
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $NANO_API_KEY" \\
  -H 'content-type: application/json' \\
  -d '{
    "slug": "nightly-report",
    "cron": "0 3 * * *",
    "timezone": "Europe/Oslo",
    "url": "https://api.example.com/jobs/nightly-report"
  }'`;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title={`NanoRelay — ${SITE_TITLE}`}
			description="NanoRelay calls your endpoint on a schedule, in your timezone, with retries and alerts when it fails. Cron without a server."
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<section class="hero">
				<div>
					<p class="eyebrow">nano-api / relay</p>
					<h1>Cron, without<br /><span class="dim">a machine to keep alive.</span></h1>
					<p class="lede">
						We call your endpoint on a schedule — in your timezone, with retries and a Slack alert
						when it starts failing.
					</p>
					<p class="cta">
						<a class="button" href="/howto/#setup">Get a free API key</a>
						<a class="button secondary" href="/howto/#relay">Curl walkthrough</a>
					</p>
					<p class="fineprint muted">
						Free, and signup is one unauthenticated <code>curl</code> — no form, no card, no wait.
					</p>
				</div>
				<RelayDemo />
			</section>

			<section class="band">
				<h2>One call to set it up</h2>
				<pre><code>{create}</code></pre>
				<p class="muted small">
					Optional: <code>body</code>, <code>headers</code>, <code>timeout_seconds</code>,
					<code>max_attempts</code>, <code>alert_webhook_url</code>. Test it with
					<code>POST /v1/schedules/:slug/run</code>.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="band">
				<h2>03:00 means 03:00, in March and in November</h2>
				<p>
					Platform crons run in UTC, so a 03:00 job quietly moves twice a year. Relay evaluates the
					expression in the zone you name.
				</p>
				<div class="two">
					<div class="card">
						<p class="tag">UTC-only cron</p>
						<ul class="plain">
							<li>Drifts an hour twice a year</li>
							<li>Skips the run when the local hour does not exist</li>
							<li>Can run twice on the ambiguous hour</li>
						</ul>
					</div>
					<div class="card alive-edge">
						<p class="tag live">NanoRelay</p>
						<ul class="plain">
							<li><code>0 3 * * *</code> in <code>Europe/Oslo</code> stays at 03:00</li>
							<li>A missing hour runs just after the gap</li>
							<li>An ambiguous hour runs once, on its first instant</li>
						</ul>
					</div>
				</div>
				<p class="muted small">All three are pinned by tests in the repo.</p>
			</section>

			<section class="band">
				<h2>When the call fails</h2>
				<ol class="steps">
					<li>
						<span class="n">1</span>
						<h3>Retry</h3>
						<p>Three attempts, 2s and 6s backoff, each bounded by your timeout.</p>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="n">2</span>
						<h3>Alert on the change</h3>
						<p>Once when it breaks, once when it recovers. Never one per failed run.</p>
					</li>
					<li>
						<span class="n">3</span>
						<h3>Keep the evidence</h3>
						<p>Status code, duration, attempts, and the start of the response body.</p>
					</li>
				</ol>
				<p class="muted small">
					Delivery is at-least-once, so make the endpoint idempotent — every request carries
					<code>X-NanoRelay-Run-Id</code>. Missed slots are skipped, not replayed: no catch-up
					stampede after an outage.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="band">
				<h2>Pairs with the others</h2>
				<p>
					Take a <a href="/lock/">Lock</a> at the top of the job and ping
					<a href="/pulse/">Pulse</a> at the end. Then a scheduler that dies quietly is still an
					alert.
				</p>
				<p class="cta">
					<a class="button" href="/howto/">How to, in curl</a>
					<a class="button secondary" href="/pricing/">What it costs</a>
				</p>
			</section>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	.hero {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1.05fr 1fr;
		gap: 2.5em;
		align-items: center;
		padding: 2em 0 1em;
	}
	.dim {
		color: var(--muted);
	}
	.lede {
		font-size: 1.1rem;
		color: var(--muted);
		max-width: 34em;
	}
	.cta {
		display: flex;
		gap: 0.7em;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		margin: 1.4em 0 0.6em;
	}
	.fineprint {
		font-size: 0.85rem;
	}
	.band {
		padding: 3em 0 0;
	}
	.band > p {
		max-width: 46em;
		color: var(--muted);
	}
	.small {
		font-size: 0.85rem;
	}
	.two {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
		gap: 1.2em;
		margin: 1.4em 0 1em;
	}
	.alive-edge {
		border-color: var(--alive-dim);
	}
	ul.plain {
		list-style: none;
		margin: 1em 0 0;
		padding: 0;
		font-size: 0.95rem;
	}
	ul.plain li {
		padding-left: 1.3em;
		position: relative;
		margin-bottom: 0.6em;
		color: var(--muted);
	}
	ul.plain li::before {
		content: "·";
		position: absolute;
		left: 0.3em;
	}
	.alive-edge ul.plain li::before {
		content: "✓";
		color: var(--alive);
		left: 0;
	}
	.steps {
		list-style: none;
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
		gap: 1.2em;
		margin: 1.4em 0 0;
		padding: 0;
	}
	.steps li {
		border-top: 2px solid var(--border);
		padding-top: 1em;
	}
	.steps .n {
		font-family: var(--mono);
		color: var(--alive-ink);
		font-size: 0.8rem;
	}
	.steps h3 {
		font-size: 1.05rem;
		margin: 0.2em 0 0.4em;
	}
	.steps p {
		color: var(--muted);
		font-size: 0.93rem;
		margin: 0;
	}
	@media (max-width: 860px) {
		.hero,
		.two,
		.steps {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}
	}
</style>
